{:edb/db-before-t 1260 :edb/db-after-t 1261 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534573 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:21:45.915Z" 13194139534573 true] [17592186198154 1100 "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" 13194139534573 true] [17592186198154 1100 "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t,\\cos t, t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4$." 13194139534573 false] [17592186198154 1145 "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(t) &= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(\\sin t), \\frac{d}{dt}(\\cos t), \\frac{d}{dt}(t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\cos t,-\\sin t, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right)\n$$\n\nwe substitute\n\n$$\nt=\\dfrac{\\pi}4\n$$\n\ninto the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(\\frac{π}{4}) &= ⟨\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}),-\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}), 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534573 false] [17592186198154 1145 "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534573 true] [17592186198157 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" 13194139534573 true] [17592186198157 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle$, what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$?" 13194139534573 false] [17592186198157 1145 "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4$, we have\n$x'(t) = 40t^3$,\nand therefore\n$x'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5$.\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t$, we have\n$y^{′}(t) = \\frac{6}{t}$,\nand therefore\n$y'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12$.\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) &= ⟨x^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}), y^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5, 12⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534573 false] [17592186198157 1145 "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534573 true] [17592186198158 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle$, Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t)$." 13194139534573 false] [17592186198158 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" 13194139534573 true] [17592186198158 1145 "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6$, we have\n$x^{′}(t)|= 6t^{5}; x^{″}(t)|= 30t^{4}$.\n- For $y(t) = t^5$, we have\n$y^{′}(t)|= 5t^{4}; y^{″}(t)|= 20t^{3}$.\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{″}(t) &= ⟨x^{″}(t), y^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨30t^{4}, 20t^{3}⟩ \\\\\n&= 10⟨3t^{4}, 2t^{3}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534573 false] [17592186198158 1145 "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534573 true] [17592186198282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296313 13194139534573 true] [17592186198282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296324 13194139534573 true] [17592186198282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296330 13194139534573 true] [17592186198282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296337 13194139534573 true] [17592186198282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296344 13194139534573 true] [17592186198283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296278 13194139534573 true] [17592186198283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296292 13194139534573 true] [17592186198283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296351 13194139534573 true] [17592186198283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296358 13194139534573 true] [17592186198283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296365 13194139534573 true] [17592186198400 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296285 13194139534573 true] [17592186198400 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296299 13194139534573 true] [17592186198400 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296306 13194139534573 true] [17592186198400 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296316 13194139534573 true] [17592186198400 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296372 13194139534573 true] [17592186296278 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296279 13194139534573 true] [17592186296278 1089 "q-123167" 13194139534573 true] [17592186296278 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534573 true] [17592186296278 1100 "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" 13194139534573 true] [17592186296278 1113 #uuid "8f7fd91d-2382-5008-942f-17ee55f68071" 13194139534573 true] [17